00:04:16,666 --> 00:04:22,666
More fun than you can shake your stick at!

2
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:39,333
Loose Screws is a comedy film directed by Rafal Zielinski.

3
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:56,000
What happens when four high school screw-ups are forced to
attend an academy summer school to graduate?

4
00:17:06,666 --> 00:17:12,666
They turn their scholastic sentence into a wacky game
of trying to improve their scores...

5
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:29,333
with the women.

6
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:46,000
The ultimate conquest for the 100-point prize is the sexy new French teacher, but
she proves to be a bigger challenge than their failing grades.

7
00:29:56,666 --> 00:30:02,666
The unforgiving principal foils every scheme, and their sidesplitting
last chance is the academy's anniversary celebration.

8
00:34:13,333 --> 00:34:19,333
Brad Lovett, played by Bryan Genesse.

9
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Steve Hardman, played by Lance Van Der Kolk.

10
00:42:46,666 --> 00:42:52,666
Hugh G. Rection, played by Alan Deveau.

11
00:47:03,333 --> 00:47:09,333
Marvin Eatmore, played by Jason Warren.

12
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Mona Lott, played by Cynthia Belliveau.

13
00:55:36,666 --> 00:55:42,666
Principal Arsenault, played by Mike MacDonald.

14
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:59,333
Screwballs II, also known as Loose Screws, is a
1985 Canadian teen sex comedy film.

15
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
It is a sequel to Screwballs and was one of the first
releases from Roger Corman's Concorde Pictures.

16
01:08:26,666 --> 01:08:32,666
The film explores themes of cheerleader, bikini, sequel, sex comedy, voyeur.

17
01:12:43,333 --> 01:12:49,333
The tone is lighthearted.
